WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
In Belgium, the number 90 is «nonante».

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.190
One short word.

3
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.370
Cross into France, and 90
becomes «quatre-vingt-dix».

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.850
And 99? «quatre-vingt-dix-neuf».

5
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.140
Four, twenty, ten, nine.

6
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.720
Why would anyone build a number like that?

7
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.940
And once you can count,

8
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.410
how do you give a date or a time?

9
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.840
In this mission, you'll stack
number blocks until 99 makes sense.

10
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.420
Then you'll build numbers
from chips in the lab,

11
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.920
flip a calendar page and
read two different clocks.

12
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.790
Your mission: crack the
French number system,

13
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.330
then give any date and
time without a slip.
